{"step_index":155,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:19:53Z","input_tokens":292,"cache_read_tokens":85760,"output_tokens":7260,"content":"Now let me apply all the fixes. I've identified a comprehensive set of bugs across all three files. Let me apply them all systematically.","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_subagent","args":{"Prompt":"You are fixing bugs in the NexusMobility app.js file at:\nC:/Users/Kartik Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/app.js\n\nRead the file fully first. Then apply ALL of the following fixes using edit_file (one edit per fix). After all edits, reply with a numbered list of every fix you applied.\n\n## FIXES TO APPLY:\n\n### FIX 1 — CRITICAL: Urban3DCanvas missing null guard on canvas (line ~363)\nThe constructor does `this.ctx = this.canvas.getContext('2d')` without checking if `this.canvas` is null (unlike AmbientEcoCanvas which has a null guard). If the element is missing, this throws.\n\nIn the constructor, AFTER `this.canvas = document.getElementById(canvasId);`, ADD:\n```\n    if (!this.canvas) return;\n```\nAnd wrap the rest of the constructor body so that `this.ctx`, `initEvents()`, `resize()`, `animate()` etc. are only called if canvas exists.\n\nThe simplest way: change lines 362-388 from:\n```\n  constructor(canvasId) {\n    this.canvas = document.getElementById(canvasId);\n    this.ctx = this.canvas.getContext('2d');\n    this.wrapper = this.canvas.parentElement;\n```\nto:\n```\n  constructor(canvasId) {\n    this.canvas = document.getElementById(canvasId);\n    // FIX: Null guard — prevent crash if canvas element is missing from DOM\n    if (!this.canvas) return;\n    this.ctx = this.canvas.getContext('2d');\n    this.wrapper = this.canvas.parentElement;\n```\n\n### FIX 2 — CRITICAL: Urban3DCanvas.resize() accumulates scale transforms (line ~396)\nEvery time resize() is called, `ctx.scale(devicePixelRatio, devicePixelRatio)` is called again on top of the previous transform, causing exponential scaling. The transform must be reset first.\n\nChange:\n```\n    this.canvas.width = this.width * window.devicePixelRatio;\n    this.canvas.height = this.height * window.devicePixelRatio;\n    this.ctx.scale(window.devicePixelRatio, window.devicePixelRatio);\n```\nto:\n```\n    this.canvas.width = this.width * window.devicePixelRatio;\n    this.canvas.height = this.height * window.devicePixelRatio;\n    // FIX: Reset transform before applying scale to prevent accumulation on repeated resize calls\n    this.ctx.setTransform(window.devicePixelRatio, 0, 0, window.devicePixelRatio, 0, 0);\n```\n\n### FIX 3 — MAJOR: Dijkstra returns empty path when origin === destination (line ~76-137)\nIf `startId === endId`, Dijkstra sets `dist[startId]=0`, the while loop immediately breaks (since `u === endId`), and the path reconstruction produces `[startId]` — a single-node path. This silently generates `totalDist=0`, `estTime=0`, `fare=4.0` (base cost), and `co2Offset` based on 0 distance. The caller should be told there's no actual route.\n\nAdd at the TOP of `findOptimalEcoRoute`, before building adjacency:\n```\n    // FIX: Guard against same-origin-destination — no meaningful route exists\n    if (startId === endId) {\n      return { path: [startId], totalDist: 0, estTime: 0, co2Offset: 0, fare: 0, soloCarsSaved: 0 };\n    }\n```\n\nSo change:\n```\n  findOptimalEcoRoute(startId, endId) {\n    const adj = {};\n```\nto:\n```\n  findOptimalEcoRoute(startId, endId) {\n    // FIX: Guard against same-origin-destination — no meaningful route exists\n    if (startId === endId) {\n      return { path: [startId], totalDist: 0, estTime: 0, co2Offset: 0, fare: 0, soloCarsSaved: 0 };\n    }\n\n    const adj = {};\n```\n\n### FIX 4 — MAJOR: dispatchSharedTrip does not guard seats < 0 (line ~218)\n`driver.seats -= 1` can go below zero if called when seats is already 0. \n\nChange:\n```\n    this.activeTrips.push(trip);\n    driver.seats -= 1;\n    driver.tripsCompleted += 1;\n```\nto:\n```\n    this.activeTrips.push(trip);\n    // FIX: Clamp seats to prevent negative values\n    driver.seats = Math.max(0, driver.seats - 1);\n    driver.tripsCompleted += 1;\n```\n\n### FIX 5 — MAJOR: cancelActiveTrip does not restore driver seat count (line ~232-239)\nWhen completing/cancelling a trip via `handleCompleteTrip`, the driver's seat count is never restored. Only `revertLatestConfirmation` restores seats. The cancel function should also restore seats.\n\nChange:\n```\n  cancelActiveTrip(tripRef) {\n    const index = this.activeTrips.findIndex(t => t.tripRef === tripRef);\n    if (index !== -1) {\n      const removed = this.activeTrips.splice(index, 1)[0];\n      return removed;\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n```\nto:\n```\n  cancelActiveTrip(tripRef) {\n    const index = this.activeTrips.findIndex(t => t.tripRef === tripRef);\n    if (index !== -1) {\n      const removed = this.activeTrips.splice(index, 1)[0];\n      // FIX: Restore driver seat capacity when trip is completed/cancelled\n      const driver = this.getDriverById(removed.driverId);\n      if (driver) {\n        driver.seats = Math.min(driver.seats + 1, driver.originalSeats);\n      }\n      return removed;\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n```\n\n### FIX 6 — MAJOR: revertLatestConfirmation double-restores seats (line ~248-252)\nNow that cancelActiveTrip restores seats (Fix 5), `revertLatestConfirmation` calls `cancelActiveTrip` AND then manually restores seats again — double restore. Remove the manual seat restore from revert.\n\nChange:\n```\n      this.cancelActiveTrip(action.tripRef);\n\n      const driver = this.getDriverById(action.driverId);\n      if (driver) {\n        driver.seats = Math.min(driver.seats + 1, driver.originalSeats);\n      }\n```\nto:\n```\n      // cancelActiveTrip already restores seat capacity\n      this.cancelActiveTrip(action.tripRef);\n\n      const driver = this.getDriverById(action.driverId);\n      // FIX: Removed duplicate seat restoration — cancelActiveTrip handles it now\n```\n\n### FIX 7 — MAJOR: popFromStandby can return stale passenger reference (standby lounge)\nWhen `standbyCount === 0` but the lounge array still has stale non-null entries from a previous cycle (e.g., if there's a bug or race), `popFromStandby` correctly returns early. But we should also ensure the returned item is truly valid. This is already correct, but let's add a defensive null check.\n\nChange:\n```\n  popFromStandby() {\n    if (this.standbyCount === 0) {\n      return { success: false, message: 'Standby lounge is currently empty.' };\n    }\n    const item = this.standbyLounge[this.standbyFront];\n```\nto:\n```\n  popFromStandby() {\n    if (this.standbyCount === 0) {\n      return { success: false, message: 'Standby lounge is currently empty.' };\n    }\n    const item = this.standbyLounge[this.standbyFront];\n    // FIX: Defensive guard against corrupted standby slot\n    if (!item) {\n      this.standbyFront = (this.standbyFront + 1) % this.standbyCap;\n      this.standbyCount--;\n      return { success: false, message: 'Standby slot was unexpectedly empty. State corrected.' };\n    }\n```\n\n### FIX 8 — MAJOR: AmbientEcoCanvas has no animation frame cleanup\nThe `animate()` method fires `requestAnimationFrame` indefinitely with no stored ID for cancellation. Store the frame ID so it can be cancelled if needed.\n\nChange (in AmbientEcoCanvas class):\n```\n    this.initParticles();\n    this.animate();\n  }\n```\nto:\n```\n    this.initParticles();\n    // FIX: Store animation frame ID for potential cleanup\n    this._animFrameId = null;\n    this.animate();\n  }\n```\n\nAnd change the animate method's last line from:\n```\n    requestAnimationFrame(() => this.animate());\n```\nto:\n```\n    this._animFrameId = requestAnimationFrame(() => this.animate());\n```\n\n### FIX 9 — MAJOR: Urban3DCanvas has no animation frame cleanup\nSame issue. Store the frame ID.\n\nIn the Urban3DCanvas constructor, after `this.flowDashOffset = 0;` add:\n```\n    // FIX: Store animation frame ID for potential cleanup\n    this._animFrameId = null;\n```\n\nAnd change the animate method's last line from:\n```\n    requestAnimationFrame(() => this.animate());\n```\n(in Urban3DCanvas, around line 506)\nto:\n```\n    this._animFrameId = requestAnimationFrame(() => this.animate());\n```\n\n### FIX 10 — MINOR: flowDashOffset decrements indefinitely (line ~495)\n`this.flowDashOffset -= 0.6;` will eventually underflow to -Infinity (or at minimum cause precision issues). Wrap it.\n\nChange:\n```\n    this.flowDashOffset -= 0.6;\n```\nto:\n```\n    // FIX: Wrap flowDashOffset to prevent unbounded decrease\n    this.flowDashOffset = (this.flowDashOffset - 0.6) % 1000;\n```\n\n### FIX 11 — MINOR: project() can produce NaN with extreme z values (division by zero in FOV)\nIf `cameraDist + z2 === 0`, the FOV becomes `Infinity`, and coordinates become `NaN`.\n\nChange:\n```\n    const cameraDist = 440;\n    const fov = cameraDist / (cameraDist + z2);\n```\nto:\n```\n    const cameraDist = 440;\n    // FIX: Clamp denominator to prevent division-by-zero / NaN coordinates\n    const fov = cameraDist / Math.max(1, cameraDist + z2);\n```\n\n### FIX 12 — MINOR: Toast icon is always emerald checkmark regardless of type (line ~1206)\nThe toast always shows `fa-circle-check text-emerald` icon even for error/rose toasts.\n\nChange:\n```\n  toast.innerHTML = `<i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check text-emerald\"></i><span>${message}</span>`;\n```\nto:\n```\n  // FIX: Use appropriate icon and color per toast type\n  const iconMap = { emerald: 'fa-circle-check text-emerald', blue: 'fa-circle-info text-electric', rose: 'fa-triangle-exclamation text-rose-500', amber: 'fa-circle-exclamation text-amber-600' };\n  const iconClass = iconMap[type] || iconMap.emerald;\n  toast.innerHTML = `<i class=\"fa-solid ${iconClass}\"></i><span>${message}</span>`;\n```\n\n### FIX 13 — MINOR: renderTransitHierarchyCanvas does not null-check countPill (line ~1006-1008)\n`countPill` is used without a null guard while `canvas` has one.\n\nChange:\n```\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n  const countPill = document.getElementById('registry-count-pill');\n\n  countPill.textContent = `${engine.activeTrips.length} Active Trips`;\n```\nto:\n```\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n  const countPill = document.getElementById('registry-count-pill');\n  // FIX: Null guard for countPill element\n  if (countPill) countPill.textContent = `${engine.activeTrips.length} Active Trips`;\n```\n(Remove the standalone `countPill.textContent` line since it's now inline with the guard)\n\n### FIX 14 — MINOR: Passenger form allows duplicate pickup === drop silently when auto-dispatching\nIn the dispatch handler (btn-auto-match-trip, line ~1544), a route is calculated without checking if `passenger.pickup === passenger.drop`. Add a guard.\n\nChange:\n```\n    const route = engine.findOptimalEcoRoute(passenger.pickup, passenger.drop);\n    const matchScore = Math.floor(Math.random() * 14 + 85);\n```\nto:\n```\n    // FIX: Guard against same pickup/drop producing empty route\n    if (passenger.pickup === passenger.drop) {\n      engine.dispatchStream.unshift(passenger);\n      showPlatformToast('Cannot dispatch — passenger pickup and destination are identical.', 'rose');\n      return;\n    }\n    const route = engine.findOptimalEcoRoute(passenger.pickup, passenger.drop);\n    const matchScore = Math.floor(Math.random() * 14 + 85);\n```\n\n### FIX 15 — MINOR: Disconnected stations produce empty path silently\nAfter calculating a route, if `res.path` is empty (disconnected graph — unlikely with current data but possible if stations/corridors are modified), the UI silently shows blank data. Add a guard in `computeAndDisplayRoute`.\n\nChange:\n```\n    const res = engine.findOptimalEcoRoute(orig, dest);\n    urbanCanvasInstance.setActivePath(res.path);\n```\nto:\n```\n    const res = engine.findOptimalEcoRoute(orig, dest);\n    // FIX: Guard against disconnected stations producing empty path\n    if (res.path.length === 0) {\n      showPlatformToast('No corridor route exists between these stations.', 'rose');\n      return;\n    }\n    urbanCanvasInstance.setActivePath(res.path);\n```\n\n### FIX 16 — MINOR: Missing modal backdrop click + ESC key handling\nModals can only be closed by clicking specific buttons. Add backdrop click and ESC handlers.\n\nAt the END of the DOMContentLoaded block (before `refreshPlatformUI()` and `computeAndDisplayRoute()` at the very bottom), INSERT:\n\n```\n  // FIX: Close modals on backdrop click and ESC key press\n  [dispatchModal, reversalModal, receiptModal].forEach(modal => {\n    modal.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n      if (e.target === modal) modal.classList.add('hidden');\n    });\n  });\n  document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n    if (e.key === 'Escape') {\n      [dispatchModal, reversalModal, receiptModal].forEach(m => m.classList.add('hidden'));\n    }\n  });\n\n```\n\nFind the lines:\n```\n  // Initial Startup\n  refreshPlatformUI();\n  computeAndDisplayRoute();\n```\nand change to:\n```\n  // FIX: Close modals on backdrop click and ESC key press\n  [dispatchModal, reversalModal, receiptModal].forEach(modal => {\n    modal.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n      if (e.target === modal) modal.classList.add('hidden');\n    });\n  });\n  document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n    if (e.key === 'Escape') {\n      [dispatchModal, reversalModal, receiptModal].forEach(m => m.classList.add('hidden'));\n    }\n  });\n\n  // Initial Startup\n  refreshPlatformUI();\n  computeAndDisplayRoute();\n```\n\n### FIX 17 — MINOR: XSS via unsanitized user input in passenger/driver names\nUser-entered names are injected directly into innerHTML. Sanitize them.\n\nAdd a utility function near the top of the file, AFTER `const engine = new NexusTransitEngine();` (line 265):\n\n```\n\n// FIX: Utility to sanitize user input against XSS injection\nfunction sanitizeHTML(str) {\n  const div = document.createElement('div');\n  div.textContent = str;\n  return div.innerHTML;\n}\n```\n\nThen in the passenger request handler, change:\n```\n    const name = nameInput.value.trim() || `Commuter_${Math.floor(Math.random() * 900 + 100)}`;\n```\n(in the btn-request-ride handler)\nto:\n```\n    const name = sanitizeHTML(nameInput.value.trim()) || `Commuter_${Math.floor(Math.random() * 900 + 100)}`;\n```\n\nAnd in the driver registration handler, change:\n```\n    const name = nameInput.value.trim() || `Partner_${Math.floor(Math.random() * 900 + 100)}`;\n```\nto:\n```\n    const name = sanitizeHTML(nameInput.value.trim()) || `Partner_${Math.floor(Math.random() * 900 + 100)}`;\n```\n\nApply ALL fixes carefully. Reply with the numbered list of fixes applied.\n","Role":"App.js Bug Fixer","TypeName":"code_fixer"}},{"name":"invoke_subagent","args":{"Prompt":"You are fixing bugs in the NexusMobility styles.css and index.html files at:\n- C:/Users/Kartik Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/styles.css\n- C:/Users/Kartik Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/index.html\n\nRead both files fully first. Then apply ALL of the following fixes using edit_file. After all edits, reply with a numbered list of every fix you applied.\n\n## CSS FIXES (styles.css):\n\n### CSS FIX 1 — Tab view animation never fires\nThe `.tab-view` has `display: none` when inactive and `display: block` when `.active`. CSS transitions cannot animate from `display: none` to `display: block` — the opacity/transform transition never fires. The element just pops in.\n\nThis is a known limitation. Add `animation` to the active state to provide a visual transition instead.\n\nChange:\n```\n.tab-view.active {\n  display: block;\n  opacity: 1;\n  transform: translateY(0);\n}\n```\nto:\n```\n.tab-view.active {\n  display: block;\n  opacity: 1;\n  transform: translateY(0);\n  /* FIX: Use animation since CSS transitions can't bridge display:none → block */\n  animation: tabFadeIn 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);\n}\n```\n\nThen add a new keyframe at the end of the file (BEFORE the closing of the file, after the last `}`), append:\n```\n\n/* FIX: Tab view entrance animation */\n@keyframes tabFadeIn {\n  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); }\n  to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }\n}\n```\n\n### CSS FIX 2 — Missing .receipt-content padding in modal\nThe `#receipt-content-area` div has class `receipt-content` but there's no CSS rule for `.receipt-content`. The receipt items display without proper spacing.\n\nAdd this rule AFTER the `.modal-dialog-body` rule block (after the `}` that closes `.modal-dialog-body` around line 1496):\n```\n\n/* FIX: Missing receipt content container styling */\n.receipt-content {\n  padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 0.65rem;\n}\n```\n\n### CSS FIX 3 — z-index stacking issue: toast container below modals\nThe `.toast-container` has `z-in